markov-cero — SIH26119 Indigenous GPU-Accelerated Optimization Solver
Copyright 2026 markov-cero contributors

This software contains clean-room C++20 implementations of:
- Continuous Linear Programming (LP) solvers:
  * Primal revised simplex with Bland's rule anti-cycling
  * Dual revised simplex with Harris ratio test, basis serialization, and warm-starts
  * Sparse basis LU factorization with product-form Eta updates
  * Matrix-free First-Order Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient (PDLP/PDHG)
- GPU-Accelerated First-Order LP Solver (CUDA):
  * Device-resident matrix-free PDHG iteration with zero in-loop transfers
  * Custom CSR SpMV and transpose-SpMV kernels with warp shuffle reduction
  * Deterministic two-stage parallel reductions for vector operations
  * Adaptive restarts, adaptive step sizes, and four-part timing telemetry
- Mixed-Integer Linear Programming (MILP) branch-and-cut solvers:
  * Sequential branch-and-cut and multithreaded parallel tree search
  * Simplex tableau Gomory Mixed-Integer (GMI) cuts with slack substitution
  * Mixed-Integer Rounding (MIR) cuts with cosine-similarity filtering
  * Strong branching lookahead evaluation, domain reduction, and pseudo-costs
  * Primal heuristics (simple rounding and feasibility pump)
- Convex Quadratic Programming (QP) & Mixed-Integer QP (MIQP):
  * OSQP-style operator-splitting ADMM over symmetric quasi-definite KKT system
  * Timothy Davis sparse LDLᵀ factorization with exact symbolic fill-in
  * Robust convexity validation via LDLᵀ diagonal pivot inspection
  * Independent zero-trust KKT certificate verifier (residuals & complementarity)
  * MPS parser support for QUADOBJ and QMATRIX quadratic sections
- Reversible LP presolve reductions, postsolve reconstruction, and Ruiz scaling
- Zero-trust dual-gated verification (canonical and original model space)

Explicit Prototype Limitations:
- Machine learning-assisted branching is not implemented in this version (planned for Phase 7).
- Dual steepest-edge recurrence is not implemented (planned for Phase 8).
